# Milestone Escrow on Soroban — Architecture and Skeleton

## Architecture

**State machine per milestone**, not one global escrow state — each milestone has an independent lifecycle: `Pending → Funded → {Approved → Released} | {Disputed → Resolved} | {Expired → Claimed}`. This lets partial funding/release happen milestone-by-milestone rather than all-or-nothing.

**Roles:** `buyer` (funder), `seller` (payee), optional `arbiter` (dispute resolver). All three are `Address` values set once at deploy via `__constructor`, which runs atomically and can't be front-run or re-invoked — the documented reason to prefer it over a guarded `initialize` (source: `skills.stellar-dev.smart-contracts` development.md, "Constructors").

**Token-agnostic funds movement.** Use `soroban_sdk::token::TokenClient` against a stored `token: Address` rather than hardcoding an asset. This works for any SEP-41-conformant token, including a Stellar Asset Contract (SAC) wrapping a classic asset like USDC. TokenClient auth pattern: `transfer` auths the `from` side, so `fund_milestone` must call `buyer.require_auth()` before pulling funds — reads need no auth (source: development.md "Tokens from the contract side"; SEP-41 spec https://developers.stellar.org/docs/tokens).

**Storage split:**
- `instance()` for small fixed config (`buyer`, `seller`, `arbiter`, `token`) — one TTL bump covers it all, capped at 64KB.
- `persistent()` keyed per milestone (`DataKey::Milestone(u32)`) — unbounded count, per-entry TTL, survives archival with restoration.

This mirrors the documented "Strategy 1 (singleton config in instance) + Strategy 2 (one entry per entity via DataKey enum)" composition (source: https://developers.stellar.org/docs/build/guides/storage/storage-strategies).

**Timeout safety valve.** Each milestone stores a `deadline_ledger: u32`. If the buyer never approves or disputes, the seller can `claim_timeout` after the deadline and pull funds without buyer cooperation — this avoids indefinite fund-lock, a known production gap in naive escrow designs. TTL itself is explicitly *not* a security or deadline mechanism (anyone can extend any entry's TTL) — the deadline must be stored as data and checked against `env.ledger().timestamp()`, per the skill's TTL guidance (source: development.md "Two facts that surprise people").

**Auth-tree discipline.** Every privileged path re-`require_auth()`s the correct stored address (not a caller-supplied one) — `approve_milestone` auths `buyer`, `resolve_dispute` auths `arbiter`, `claim_timeout` needs no auth (anyone can trigger it, funds always go to `seller`). This follows the #1 real-world Soroban auth bug pattern documented in `security.md`: "the right address matters more than the call itself."

**Reentrancy** is host-blocked on Soroban (no `delegatecall`, no reentrant calls) but state is still updated *before* the token transfer (checks-effects-interactions) per the security checklist's "Check-then-act races" guidance.

### Prior art (read, don't clone)
- **Trustless-Work/trustlesswork-smart-contract-stellar** — https://github.com/Trustless-Work/trustlesswork-smart-contract-stellar — "permissionless escrow infrastructure... leverages Stellar Soroban Smart Contracts and USDC." Maintained activity state, repoScore 62. Closest production analog for milestone-based escrow; worth reading their milestone/dispute state machine before finalizing yours. License/audit status unverified from this search — check the repo directly.
- **workvault-hq/workvault** — https://github.com/workvault-hq/workvault — "Milestone-based freelance marketplace escrow on Stellar + Soroban," repoScore 33 (lower signal, but same domain shape).

## Contract skeleton

```rust
#![no_std]
use soroban_sdk::{
    contract, contracterror, contractevent, contractimpl, contracttype,
    token::TokenClient, Address, Env, Vec,
};

#[contracttype]
#[derive(Clone)]
pub enum DataKey {
    Buyer,
    Seller,
    Arbiter,
    Token,
    MilestoneCount,
    Milestone(u32),
}

#[contracttype]
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Eq, PartialEq)]
pub enum MilestoneStatus {
    Pending,   // created, not yet funded
    Funded,    // buyer's tokens are held by the contract
    Released,  // paid out to seller
    Disputed,  // either party flagged it; awaiting arbiter
    Refunded,  // arbiter or cancellation returned funds to buyer
}

#[contracttype]
#[derive(Clone)]
pub struct Milestone {
    pub amount: i128,
    pub status: MilestoneStatus,
    pub deadline_ledger: u32, // ledger seq after which seller may claim unilaterally
}

#[contracterror]
#[derive(Copy, Clone, Debug, Eq, PartialEq)]
#[repr(u32)]
pub enum Error {
    NotInitialized = 1,
    InvalidAmount = 2,
    MilestoneNotFound = 3,
    WrongStatus = 4,
    DeadlineNotReached = 5,
    DeadlineInPast = 6,
}

#[contractevent]
pub struct MilestoneFunded {
    #[topic]
    pub milestone_id: u32,
    pub amount: i128,
}

#[contractevent]
pub struct MilestoneReleased {
    #[topic]
    pub milestone_id: u32,
    pub to: Address,
}

#[contractevent]
pub struct MilestoneDisputed {
    #[topic]
    pub milestone_id: u32,
    pub raised_by: Address,
}

#[contractevent]
pub struct MilestoneResolved {
    #[topic]
    pub milestone_id: u32,
    pub buyer_share: i128,
    pub seller_share: i128,
}

#[contract]
pub struct MilestoneEscrow;

#[contractimpl]
impl MilestoneEscrow {
    /// Runs once at deploy. Milestone amounts and per-milestone deadlines
    /// (ledger sequence, not wall-clock) are fixed at creation.
    pub fn __constructor(
        env: Env,
        buyer: Address,
        seller: Address,
        arbiter: Address,
        token: Address,
        amounts: Vec<i128>,
        deadlines: Vec<u32>,
    ) {
        env.storage().instance().set(&DataKey::Buyer, &buyer);
        env.storage().instance().set(&DataKey::Seller, &seller);
        env.storage().instance().set(&DataKey::Arbiter, &arbiter);
        env.storage().instance().set(&DataKey::Token, &token);
        env.storage().instance().set(&DataKey::MilestoneCount, &amounts.len());

        for i in 0..amounts.len() {
            let m = Milestone {
                amount: amounts.get(i).unwrap(),
                status: MilestoneStatus::Pending,
                deadline_ledger: deadlines.get(i).unwrap(),
            };
            env.storage().persistent().set(&DataKey::Milestone(i), &m);
        }
        env.storage().instance().extend_ttl(120 * 17280, 180 * 17280);
    }

    /// Buyer funds one milestone. Pulls tokens into contract custody.
    pub fn fund_milestone(env: Env, milestone_id: u32) -> Result<(), Error> {
        let buyer: Address = env.storage().instance().get(&DataKey::Buyer).unwrap();
        buyer.require_auth();

        let mut m = Self::get_milestone(&env, milestone_id)?;
        if m.status != MilestoneStatus::Pending {
            return Err(Error::WrongStatus);
        }

        let token_addr: Address = env.storage().instance().get(&DataKey::Token).unwrap();
        let token = TokenClient::new(&env, &token_addr);
        token.transfer(&buyer, &env.current_contract_address(), &m.amount);

        m.status = MilestoneStatus::Funded;
        env.storage().persistent().set(&DataKey::Milestone(milestone_id), &m);
        env.storage().persistent().extend_ttl(&DataKey::Milestone(milestone_id), 30 * 17280, 120 * 17280);

        MilestoneFunded { milestone_id, amount: m.amount }.publish(&env);
        Ok(())
    }

    /// Buyer approves completed work; releases funds to seller.
    pub fn approve_milestone(env: Env, milestone_id: u32) -> Result<(), Error> {
        let buyer: Address = env.storage().instance().get(&DataKey::Buyer).unwrap();
        buyer.require_auth();
        Self::release_to_seller(&env, milestone_id, MilestoneStatus::Funded)
    }

    /// Seller claims payout unilaterally once the deadline has passed
    /// without buyer approval or dispute. Prevents indefinite fund-lock.
    pub fn claim_timeout(env: Env, milestone_id: u32) -> Result<(), Error> {
        let m = Self::get_milestone(&env, milestone_id)?;
        if env.ledger().sequence() < m.deadline_ledger {
            return Err(Error::DeadlineNotReached);
        }
        Self::release_to_seller(&env, milestone_id, MilestoneStatus::Funded)
    }

    /// Either party flags a funded milestone as disputed.
    pub fn raise_dispute(env: Env, milestone_id: u32, raised_by: Address) -> Result<(), Error> {
        raised_by.require_auth();
        let buyer: Address = env.storage().instance().get(&DataKey::Buyer).unwrap();
        let seller: Address = env.storage().instance().get(&DataKey::Seller).unwrap();
        if raised_by != buyer && raised_by != seller {
            return Err(Error::WrongStatus); // not a party to this escrow
        }

        let mut m = Self::get_milestone(&env, milestone_id)?;
        if m.status != MilestoneStatus::Funded {
            return Err(Error::WrongStatus);
        }
        m.status = MilestoneStatus::Disputed;
        env.storage().persistent().set(&DataKey::Milestone(milestone_id), &m);

        MilestoneDisputed { milestone_id, raised_by }.publish(&env);
        Ok(())
    }

    /// Arbiter splits a disputed milestone's funds between buyer and seller.
    pub fn resolve_dispute(
        env: Env,
        milestone_id: u32,
        buyer_share: i128,
        seller_share: i128,
    ) -> Result<(), Error> {
        let arbiter: Address = env.storage().instance().get(&DataKey::Arbiter).unwrap();
        arbiter.require_auth();

        let mut m = Self::get_milestone(&env, milestone_id)?;
        if m.status != MilestoneStatus::Disputed {
            return Err(Error::WrongStatus);
        }
        if buyer_share < 0 || seller_share < 0 || buyer_share + seller_share != m.amount {
            return Err(Error::InvalidAmount);
        }

        m.status = MilestoneStatus::Refunded; // terminal; funds already split below
        env.storage().persistent().set(&DataKey::Milestone(milestone_id), &m);

        let token_addr: Address = env.storage().instance().get(&DataKey::Token).unwrap();
        let token = TokenClient::new(&env, &token_addr);
        let buyer: Address = env.storage().instance().get(&DataKey::Buyer).unwrap();
        let seller: Address = env.storage().instance().get(&DataKey::Seller).unwrap();
        if buyer_share > 0 {
            token.transfer(&env.current_contract_address(), &buyer, &buyer_share);
        }
        if seller_share > 0 {
            token.transfer(&env.current_contract_address(), &seller, &seller_share);
        }

        MilestoneResolved { milestone_id, buyer_share, seller_share }.publish(&env);
        Ok(())
    }

    // -- internal helpers --

    fn get_milestone(env: &Env, id: u32) -> Result<Milestone, Error> {
        env.storage()
            .persistent()
            .get(&DataKey::Milestone(id))
            .ok_or(Error::MilestoneNotFound)
    }

    fn release_to_seller(env: &Env, id: u32, expected: MilestoneStatus) -> Result<(), Error> {
        let mut m = Self::get_milestone(env, id)?;
        if m.status != expected {
            return Err(Error::WrongStatus);
        }
        m.status = MilestoneStatus::Released;
        env.storage().persistent().set(&DataKey::Milestone(id), &m);

        let token_addr: Address = env.storage().instance().get(&DataKey::Token).unwrap();
        let seller: Address = env.storage().instance().get(&DataKey::Seller).unwrap();
        let token = TokenClient::new(env, &token_addr);
        token.transfer(&env.current_contract_address(), &seller, &m.amount);

        MilestoneReleased { milestone_id: id, to: seller }.publish(env);
        Ok(())
    }
}
```

## Gaps to close before production (not yet in the skeleton)

- **No cancellation path** for a funded-but-never-approved milestone before its deadline — decide whether buyer should be able to cancel with seller consent.
- **No `total = sum(amounts)` cap check** or duplicate-deadline validation in the constructor.
- **Integer overflow** on `buyer_share + seller_share` should use `checked_add` per the security checklist's overflow-checks guidance, not raw `+`.
- **Upgradeability** is unaddressed — see `skills.openzeppelin-stellar.upgrade-stellar-contracts` if you need post-deploy fixes.
- Project setup, `Cargo.toml`, and the exact `soroban-sdk` version pin (protocol-dependent — mainnet is on protocol 26 as of this skill's writing; check crates.io for current) are in `skills.stellar-dev.smart-contracts` → `project-setup`.
- Full test methodology (unit, fuzz, mutation) is in the companion `testing.md` file of the same skill — not pulled in this pass.

Source basis: `skills.stellar-dev.smart-contracts` (development.md, security.md, contract-anatomy) at https://github.com/stellar/stellar-dev-skill; `stellarDocs.search_soroban_contract_docs` and `search_asset_token_docs` against https://developers.stellar.org/docs; prior-art repos via `scout.searchRepos`.

